## ⚙️ Environment Variables

Configure the following environment variables before running the application:

```text
SHEMS_PORT=8080

MYSQL_HOST=localhost
MYSQL_PORT=3306
MYSQL_DATABASE=shems_db
MYSQL_USERNAME=root
MYSQL_PASSWORD=

SHEMS_MAIL_USERNAME=your-email@example.com
SHEMS_MAIL_PASSWORD=your-email-password
```

### Database Configuration

Create the MySQL database:

```sql
CREATE DATABASE shems_db;
```

Update the database credentials according to your local MySQL configuration.

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

Make sure you have installed:

* Java 17+
* Maven
* MySQL
* Git

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Nathin78/Smart-Home-Energy-Management-System.git
```

### 2. Navigate to the Project

```bash
cd Smart-Home-Energy-Management-System
```

### 3. Configure MySQL

Create the database:

```sql
CREATE DATABASE shems_db;
```

Configure your MySQL username and password using the application configuration or environment variables.

### 4. Build the Project

```bash
mvn clean install
```

### 5. Run the Application

```bash
mvn spring-boot:run
```

The backend will start on:

```text
http://localhost:8080
```

